{"text":"{
  "status": "NEEDS_IMPROVEMENT",
  "core_findings": [
    "Electronics has the weakest training separation: its 10th-percentile margin is negative (-0.2994), and sampled negatives outrank positives at 13.08% of valid positions. Movies_and_TV has the strongest separation, with only 2.21% wrong rankings; Industrial_and_Scientific and CDs_and_Vinyl fall between them.",
    "Embedding alignment scores range from 0.5432 to 0.5782; these values alone do not establish representation collapse or recommendation diversity."
  ],
  "key_implications": [
    "The model ranks positives above sampled negatives at most measured training positions in every category, but Electronics shows the largest weak-separation tail.",
    "These training diagnostics do not establish validation HR@10 performance; gradient health and recent-branch behavior cannot be assessed because their measured values are absent."
  ],
  "evidence": {
    "headline_metrics": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_margin_p10": -0.2994,
      "Electronics:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": 0.1308,
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": 0.1892,
      "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": 0.0221
    },
    "brief_metric_read": {
      "Electronics:pos_neg_margin_p10": "Lower-tail positive-minus-negative margin is below zero.",
      "Electronics:pos_neg_small_margin_rate": "18.92% of valid training positions have margins below 0.5.",
      "Movies_and_TV:pos_neg_neg_beats_pos_rate": "Lowest sampled wrong-ranking rate across the four categories."
    }
  }
}"}
